  51→   - Evidence: Both refer to Henry Clerval, Victor's best friend\n    52→   - Location: Same as #4\n    53→   - Fix: Same as #4\n    54→   - Impact: -0.15 points\n    55→\n    56→6. **Nonsense character entry: \"M.\"**\n    57→   - Problem: \"M.\" listed as standalone character with 23 mentions and no description\n    58→   - Evidence: This is an incomplete name extraction - likely fragments from \"M. Waldman\", \"M. Krempe\", \"M. Frankenstein\"\n    59→   - Location: Name extraction and validation in character extraction\n    60→   - Fix: Filter out standalone titles/honorifics that aren't followed by a name. \"M.\" alone should never be a character.\n    61→   - Impact: -0.3 points\n    62→\n    63→7. **Character alias resolution failure: Caroline Frankenstein**\n    64→   - Problem: \"my mother\" (10 mentions) and \"Madame Frankenstein\" (1 mention) are separate characters\n    65→   - Evidence: Both refer to Caroline Beaufort Frankenstein, Victor's mother\n    66→   - Location: Same root cause as Critical #1\n    67→   - Fix: Same approach as Critical #1\n    68→   - Impact: -0.2 points\n    69→\n    70→### MEDIUM\n    71→8. **De Lacey fragmentation**\n    72→   - Problem: \"De Lacey\" (9 mentions), \"De\" (6 mentions), and \"old man\" (2 mentions) are separate\n    73→   - Evidence: All refer to the blind father in the cottage where the Creature learns language\n    74→   - Location: Name extraction creating incomplete \"De\" + descriptor resolution for \"old man\"\n    75→   - Fix: Improve compound name handling for \"De Lacey\", \"Van Helsing\" style names. Merge descriptive references.\n    76→   - Impact: -0.1 points\n    77→\n    78→9. **Inconsistent canonical names using possessive descriptors**\n    79→   - Problem: \"my father\", \"my mother\" used as canonical names instead of \"Alphonse Frankenstein\", \"Caroline Frankenstein\"\n    80→   - Evidence: Character profiles show \"my father\" and \"my mother\" as main headings\n    81→   - Location: 