ed to have a calming influence on the narrator's intense passions. As the narrative progresses, she becomes engaged to the narrator, and her emotional state fluctuates between joy and melancholy, particularly as the narrator's fate draws near. Her letters and actions reflect deep affection and concern for the narrator, and she remains a central figure in his emotional life until the final moments of the story.</div>\n  1502→                    \n  1503→\n  1504→                    \n  1505→                    \n  1506→\n  1507→                    \n  1508→                    <details style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem;\">\n  1509→                        <summary style=\"cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem;\">📊 Metadata</summary>\n  1510→                        <div class=\"profile-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n  1511→                            <span>90 mentions</span> •\n  1512→                            <span>First appears: Ch. 2</span> •\n  1513→                            <span class=\"tag low\">low confidence</span>\n  1514→                        </div>\n  1515→                    </details>\n  1516→                </div>\n  1517→                \n  1518→                <div class=\"character-profile character-item\" data-confidence=\"high\">\n  1519→                    <h4>\n  1520→                        Clerval\n  1521→                        \n  1522→                        \n  1523→                        <span class=\"confidence-badge high\" title=\"Confidence: high\">\n  1524→                            ✓\n  1525→                            \n  1526→                        </span>\n  1527→                    </h4>\n  1528→\n  1529→                    \n  1530→\n  1531→                    \n  1532→                    \n  1533→\n  1534→                    \n  1535→\n  1536→                    \n  1537→\n  1538→                    \n  1539→                    \n  1540→\n  1541→                