ider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07185c06-f7d4-4b27-99ad-ef3e65820d0e","uuid":"de064edd-4a57-4049-98d5-b27c84fd0d3d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/output/frankenstein/report.html","content":"            <h2>👥 Character Guide</h2>\n\n            <!-- Confidence Filter -->\n            <div style=\"margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\">\n                <label style=\"color: var(--muted); margin-right: 0.5rem;\">\n                    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"show-low-confidence-only\" onchange=\"filterByConfidence(this.checked)\">\n                    Show only low-confidence items\n                </label>\n            </div>\n\n            \n            <div class=\"character-group\">\n                <h3>Main Characters <span class=\"count\">15</span></h3>\n\n                \n                <div class=\"character-profile character-item\" data-confidence=\"low\">\n                    <h4>\n                        Elizabeth\n                        \n                        \n                        <span class=\"confidence-badge low\" title=\"Confidence: low\">\n                            ⚠\n                            \n                        </span>\n                    </h4>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n                    <div class=\"profile-body\">Elizabeth Lavenza is introduced as a fair-haired orphan of noble birth discovered by the narrator's mother in Italy and brought into the family as a foster daughter, described as the narrator's 'more than sister.' She grows up alongside the narrator and Henry Clerval in Geneva and Belrive, where her gentle nature is noted to have a calming influence on the narrator's intense passions. As the narrative progresses, she becomes engaged to the narrator, and her emotional state fluctuates between joy and melancholy, particularly as the narrator's fate draws near. Her letters and actions reflect deep affection and concern for the narrator, and she remains a central figure in his emotional life until the final moments of the story.</div>\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n\n                    \n                    <details style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem;\">\n                        <summary style=\"cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem;\">📊 Metadata</summary>\n                        <div class=\"profile-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                            <span>90 mentions</span> •\n                            <span>First appears: Ch. 2</span> •\n                            <span class=\"tag low\">low confidence</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"character-profile character-item\" data-confidence=\"high\">\n                    <h4>\n                        Clerval\n                        \n                        \n                        <span class=\"confidence-badge high\" title=\"Confidence: high\">\n                            ✓\n                            \n                        </span>\n                    </h4>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n                    <div class=\"profile-body\">Henry Clerval is portrayed as a compassionate, imaginative, and emotionally attuned individual who serves as a stabilizing presence in the narrator's life. Throughout the narrative, he is depicted as a source of comfort, care, and moral contrast, particularly during the narrator's periods of psychological distress and physical illness. His character remains consistent in his kindness and enthusiasm for life, even as the narrator descends into despair.</div>\n                    \n\n                    \n                    \n                    <details style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem;\" id=\"evidence-2\">\n                        <summary style=\"cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted);\">📑 Source Evidence (9 citations)</summary>\n                        <div class=\"chapter-details\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem;\">\n                            <ul class=\"evidence-list\">\n                                \n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-1\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval possesses a noble and humane spirit that is unaffected by ill</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-2\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is sensitive, generous, and full of kindness despite his passion for adventure</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-3\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is deeply affected by the narrator's erratic behavior upon reunion</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-4\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is present during the narrator's mental breakdown and is believed to be murdered</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-5\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is described as being joyful and responsive to beauty and new experiences</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-6\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is seen as a reflection of the narrator's former self, full of curiosity and desire for experience</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-7\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                                    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.25rem;\"><strong>Clerval is a source of comfort and healing during the narrator's illness</strong></div>\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                </li>\n                                \n                                <li class=\"evidence-item\" id=\"ev-2-8\">\n                                    <div>\n                                        <span class=\"tag\">fact</span>\n                                        \n                                    </div>\n                                    \n                               